# release-overlay.commits
#
# List the commits you want to layer on top of each upstream release tag.
# One commit SHA, short SHA, or branch ref per line. Lines starting with '#'
# are comments; blank lines are ignored. Order matters — cherry-picks run
# top-to-bottom.
#
# Re-running for a new release (e.g. v2026.8.15):
#   1. Add any NEW custom commits to this file (old ones still in the list
#      are skipped automatically if they're already on the new tag's base).
#   2. Run: scripts/release-overlay.sh v2026.8.15
#   3. Resolve any conflicts interactively. Re-run after fixing.
#   4. Push: git push fork release/v2026.8.15 jasnoor/v2026.8.15-custom
#
# --- TinyFish web backend ---
# Plugin + registry wiring. v2026.9.7's plugin-discovery model absorbs the
# old "register in legacy allowlist" and "add to schema gate" hardcodes —
# just one commit is needed now (the plugin files themselves), because
# _is_backend_available() / check_web_api_key() auto-route through the
# registry. NOT yet on any upstream release tag — this is our unique
# value-add.
3551c87986

# --- TinyFish web backend (legacy 3-commit stack, kept for history) ---
# These were the canonical 3 commits on jasnoor/v2026.8.19-custom:
#   feat(web): add tinyfish search+fetch plugin with burst-drain free-tier throttling
#   fix(web): register tinyfish plugin and add to legacy backend allowlist
#   fix(web): add tinyfish to schema gate allowlist and availability probe
# All three are obsolete against v2026.9.7+ — the registry pattern absorbed
# the second and third, and the first was superseded by 3551c87986 (clean
# port onto BaseWebSearchProvider). DO NOT uncomment: re-adding them
# conflicts with the registry-driven design (see release-overlay gotcha:
# "Conflict pattern when upstream refactored a function you patched").
# 71ccbe3d03
# 2866a26851
# a449637f3f

